    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "6ea1df1f",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Paso 6 - Dividir entrenamiento y prueba\n",
        "\n",
        "Se utiliza una división de **75 % para entrenamiento y 25 % para prueba**, siguiendo la proporción del ejercicio guiado.\n",
        "\n",
        "`stratify=y` mantiene una proporción similar de las clases en ambos conjuntos.\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 7,
      "id": "376b562a",
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [
        {
          "name": "stdout",
          "output_type": "stream",
          "text": [
            "Tamaño X_train: (426, 30)\n",
            "Tamaño X_test: (143, 30)\n",
            "\n",
            "Distribución train:\n",
            "diagnostico\n",
            "0    267\n",
            "1    159\n",
            "Name: count, dtype: int64\n",
            "\n",
            "Distribución test:\n",
            "diagnostico\n",
            "0    90\n",
            "1    53\n",
            "Name: count, dtype: int64\n"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "X_train, X_test, y_train, y_test = train_test_split(\n",
        "    X,\n",
        "    y,\n",
        "    test_size=0.25,\n",
        "    random_state=42,\n",
        "    stratify=y\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"Tamaño X_train:\", X_train.shape)\n",
        "print(\"Tamaño X_test:\", X_test.shape)\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"\\nDistribución train:\")\n",
        "print(y_train.value_counts().sort_index())\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"\\nDistribución test:\")\n",
        "print(y_test.value_counts().sort_index())\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "c6c57370",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Paso adicional - Estandarizar las variables\n",
        "\n",
        "\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 8,
      "id": "4559d7c2",
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [
        {
          "name": "stdout",
          "output_type": "stream",
          "text": [
            "Estandarización completada.\n",
            "Número de variables estandarizadas: 30\n"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "escalador = StandardScaler()\n",
        "\n",
        "X_train_scaled = escalador.fit_transform(X_train)\n",
        "X_test_scaled = escalador.transform(X_test)\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"Estandarización completada.\")\n",
        "print(\"Número de variables estandarizadas:\", X_train_scaled.shape[1])\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "91782186",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Paso 7 - Crear y entrenar el modelo\n",
        "\n",
        "Se utiliza `LogisticRegression` para resolver la clasificación binaria. `max_iter=1000` permite suficientes iteraciones para que el algoritmo alcance la convergencia con las 30 variables.\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 9,
      "id": "6e5cb3a3",
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [
        {
          "name": "stdout",
          "output_type": "stream",
          "text": [
            "Modelo entrenado correctamente.\n"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "modelo = LogisticRegression(\n",
        "    max_iter=1000,\n",
        "    random_state=42\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "modelo.fit(X_train_scaled, y_train)\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"Modelo entrenado correctamente.\")\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "bddc1a25",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Paso 8 - Predecir clases y probabilidades\n",
        "\n",
        "Se generan dos tipos de resultado:\n",
        "\n",
        "- `predict()` entrega la clase final.\n",
        "- `predict_proba()` entrega la probabilidad estimada para cada clase.\n",
        "\n",
        "La segunda columna de `predict_proba()` corresponde a la probabilidad de la clase 1, es decir, **maligno**.\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 10,
      "id": "632b5ed2",
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [
        {
